{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_f8c4b83d413c",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 10177,
      "mechanism": "The patch qualifies an EXPAND_BUS condition with input_axis_tlast. During frame tailing in expand mode, the original unqualified condition allowed the state machine to request new input data while still holding the last output beat, causing the output pipeline to stall with output_axis_tvalid incorrectly deasserted (observed cycle 9: expected 0, actual 1). Adding the tlast gate prevents this premature input request."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_e1b071d54052",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 5165,
      "mechanism": "The patch adds input_axis_tvalid to the CYCLE_COUNT==1 branch. When a single-cycle transfer arrives without valid, the original code still drove input_axis_tready based on output_axis_tready_int_early, asserting ready (cycle 8 expected 1, actual 0). Gating with tvalid ensures ready only rises when a valid word is present."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_2a85c0d2ad99",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tlast",
      "source_line": 6503,
      "mechanism": "The patch qualifies the input_axis_tlast check with output_axis_tready_int in the EXPAND_BUS transfer-in path. Without this, the state machine could advance to TRANSFER_OUT while the output side was not ready, causing output_axis_tlast to deassert early (cycle 8 expected 1, actual 0). The gate aligns the frame boundary with output readiness."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_4da73638e1ac",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 9435,
      "mechanism": "The patch adds output_axis_tready_int to the cycle-count/last-word completion condition in the shrink path (STATE_TRANSFER_OUT). The original condition could declare the frame done and drop output_axis_tvalid while the output skid buffer was still holding data, producing the extra valid beat at cycle 9. The gate keeps valid asserted until the output side accepts the last word."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_7d6c69bf2e61",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tlast",
      "source_line": 8232,
      "mechanism": "The patch qualifies the EXPAND_BUS input-consumption condition with input_axis_tvalid. In expand mode, the original code could consume a new input word based solely on output_axis_tready_int, even when input was not valid, corrupting the frame boundary and causing output_axis_tlast mismatch at cycle 8."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_b689ecffefee",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 6503,
      "mechanism": "The patch adds input_axis_tvalid to the same input_axis_tlast condition in the EXPAND_BUS transfer-in path. This prevents the state machine from treating an invalid beat as a frame terminator, which otherwise would cause premature transition and the extra output_axis_tvalid at cycle 9."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_628ff018d189",
      "failure_port": "output_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 8922,
      "mechanism": "The patch qualifies the early readiness expression with !output_axis_tready_int. The original early-ready signal could assert when the output skid buffer was still occupied, allowing the state machine to pull new data and drop output_axis_tvalid one cycle early (cycle 9 mismatch)."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_f927a53d2b54",
      "failure_port": "input_axis_tready",
      "source_line": 9435,
      "mechanism": "The patch adds !input_axis_tvalid to the shrink-path completion condition. This prevents the state machine from completing a transfer cycle on an invalid input beat, which could otherwise cause input_axis_tready to deassert incorrectly (cycle 8 expected 1, actual 0)."
    }
  ]

  ,
  "explanation": "The three observed mismatches (input_axis_tready at cycle 8, output_axis_tlast at cycle 8, output_axis_tvalid at cycle 9) all stem from the state machine advancing or holding based on partial handshake information. In expand mode (64->8), the frame tail requires the output skid buffer to fully drain before new input is requested; in shrink mode (8->64), the last output word must stay valid until output_axis_tready_int accepts it. The top-ranked patches gate the critical EXPAND_BUS and CYCLE_COUNT conditions with the missing scalar signals (tlast, tvalid, output_axis_tready_int) that were observed in the failing trace but not present in the original conditions. Lower-ranked patches address the same root causes on adjacent condition sites. The ranking orders patches by proximity to the exact cycle/expression where the trace diverges."
}
